expected_issues.description:
Potential compatibility/runtime risk: this change assumes `this.db.statusPageModule` always exists and exposes `deleteStatusPage`. If `this.db` is sometimes a direct module (as before) or initialization differs across environments/tests, this will throw (cannot read property 'deleteStatusPage' of undefined). Consider adding a null-safe guard with a clear error, or keep backward compatibility by falling back to `this.db.deleteStatusPage` when `statusPageModule` is absent. Also consider validating `req.params.url` is present/expected format before passing to DB layer.

```suggestion
   const { url } = req.params;
   if (!url) {
     return res.badRequest({ msg: 'Missing status page url' });
   }
   const mod = this.db.statusPageModule ?? this.db;
   if (typeof mod.deleteStatusPage !== 'function') {
     throw new Error('deleteStatusPage is not available on db module');
   }
   await mod.deleteStatusPage(url);
```

