`runMigrations()` is executed *after* `logger.info('Connected...')`. If migrations fail, logs will still claim successful readiness, which can mislead operators and health checks. Consider running migrations before emitting the success log, or log a separate "Migrations completed" message after success (and/or "Starting migrations" before).

```suggestion
			this.logger.info({
				message: "Connected to MongoDB, starting migrations",
				service: this.SERVICE_NAME,
				method: "connect",
			});

			await runMigrations();

			this.logger.info({
				message: "MongoDB migrations completed",
				service: this.SERVICE_NAME,
				method: "connect",
			});
```

