Missing error handling and null checks. It is recommended to add:
1. Null check for the monitor parameter to avoid null pointer exceptions
2. Add try-catch error handling, consistent with the pauseJob and resumeJob methods
3. Add debug log recording to facilitate troubleshooting

```suggestion
 updateJob = async (monitor) => {
 		if (!monitor) {
 			throw new Error("Monitor parameter is required");
 		}
 		try {
 			const result = this.scheduler.updateJob(monitor._id.toString(), { repeat: monitor.interval, data: monitor.toObject() });
 			if (result === false) {
 				throw new Error("Failed to update monitor");
 			}
 			this.logger.debug({
 				message: `Updated monitor ${monitor._id}`,
 				service: SERVICE_NAME,
 				method: "updateJob",
 			});
 		} catch (error) {
 			this.logger.error({
 				message: "Failed to update monitor",
 				service: SERVICE_NAME,
 				method: "updateJob",
 				details: error,
 			});
 			throw error;
 		}
 	};
```

